03,47384443,47386300,47384871,47385453,47384105,47384194],"score":275,"time":1773525827,"title":"Allow me to get to know you, mistakes and all","type":"story","url":"https://sebi.io/posts/2026-03-14-allow-me-to-get-to-know-you-mistakes-and-all/"},{"by":"bookofjoe","descendants":4,"id":47348502,"kids":[47363449,47389674,47387235],"score":65,"time":1773309348,"title":"Human Organ Atlas","type":"story","url":"https://www.science.org/doi/10.1126/sciadv.adz2240"},{"by":"ibobev","descendants":7,"id":47334668,"kids":[47387095,47386783,47387725,47386728],"score":75,"time":1773231849,"title":"Examples for the tcpdump and dig man pages","type":"story","url":"https://jvns.ca/blog/2026/03/10/examples-for-the-tcpdump-and-dig-man-pages/"},{"by":"pentagrama","descendants":3,"id":47389292,"kids":[47390476,47390548,47390140],"score":30,"time":1773594035,"title":"SuperTux 0.7.0","type":"story","url":"https://github.com/SuperTux/supertux/releases/tag/v0.7.0"},{"by":"bryanrasmussen","descendants":1,"id":47390176,"kids":[47390411],"score":7,"time":1773598719,"title":"Da Vinci's Largest Collection of Drawings and Writings Digitized","type":"story","url":"https://mymodernmet.com/leonardo-da-vinci-codex-atlanticus-the-visual-agency-database/"},{"by":"bensouthwood","descendants":45,"id":47337423,"kids":[47387011,47384554,47387010,47385656,47386913,47388857,47388485,47388914,47389147,47384861,47337766,47387460,47384787,47384856,47384896,47385881,47386791],"score":117,"time":1773245220,"title":"Centuries of selective breeding turned wild cabbage into different vegetables","type":"story","url":"https://www.worksinprogress.news/p/many-of-the-tastiest-vegetables-are"},{"by":"xodn348","descendants":112,"id":47381382,"kids":[47383386,47382219,47386312,47382747,47390269,47387950,47387378,47382246,47382765,47384290,47389946,47381772,47382790,47389831,47383946,47383450,47385021,47382348,47383111,47382365,47382498,47383189,47382806,47383383,47384366,47385261,47382930,47383080,47385048,47383509,47382272,47386617,47383261,47385832,47382656,47382635,47382899,47382832,47384017,47387017,47382451,47390005,47385153,47381630,47386266,47386152,47381993],"score":201,"text":"A few weeks ago I saw a post about someone converting an entire C++ codebase to Rust using AI in under two weeks.<p>That inspired me — if AI can rewrite a whole language stack that fast, I wanted to try building a programming language from scratch with AI assistance.<p>I&#x27;ve also been noticing growing global interest in Korean language and culture, and I wondered: what would a programming language look like if every keyword was in Hangul (the Korean writing system)?<p>Han is the result. It&#x27;s a statically-typed language written in Rust with a full compiler pipeline (lexer → parser → AST → interpreter + LLVM IR codegen).<p>It supports arrays, structs with impl blocks, closures, pattern matching, try&#x2F;catch, file I&#x2F;O, module imports, a REPL, and a basic LSP server.<p>This is a side project, not a &quot;you should use this instead of Python&quot; pitch. \nFeedback on language design, compiler architecture, or the Korean keyword choices is very welcome.<p><a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;xodn348&#x2F;han\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;xodn348&#x2F;han</a>","time":1773523653,"title":"Show HN: Han – A Korean programming language written in Rust","type":"story","url":"https://github.com/xodn348/han"},{"by":"anonzzzies","descendants":29,"id":47382398,"kids":[47387121,47384693,47384503,47383871,47383008,47384813,47384317,47382933,47384631],"score":138,"time":1773530559,"title":"SBCL Fibers – Lightweight Cooperative Threads","type":"story","url":"https://atgreen.github.io/repl-yell/posts/sbcl-fibers/"},{"by":"geox","descendants":72,"id":47386651,"kids":[47387177,47388567,47387556,47387386,47388843,47389000,47387789,47389069,47387444,47389263,47389157,47388357,47389562,47387958,47389206,47388115,47387608],"score":153,"time":1773576692,"title":"Pentagon expands ove